{"id":"standard","name":"Rwandan tax resident","type":"standard","description":"Worldwide PIT 0-30%; 15% final WHT on dividends and interest; 10% CGT on shares.","eligible_citizenships":["EU","US","OTHER"],"eligibility":"Resident with a permanent residence or habitual abode in Rwanda, more than 183 days in any 12-month period, or an average of more than 122 days in each of the two preceding tax periods while present in the year. Foreigners need a residence permit.","duration_years":null,"requires_qualifying_activity":false,"duration_note":"","lump_sum":null,"structure":null,"capital_gains":{"status":"researched","basis":"law_in_force","summary":"CGT of 10% applies to the gain on the direct or indirect sale or transfer of shares, debt instruments, options and similar assets. Gains on listed shares and securities sold on the capital market, and on units of collective investment schemes, are exempt. Gains on commercial immovable property are taxed at 30%. Residents are taxed on worldwide income, so foreign share gains are scored at 10%.","exemptions_thresholds":"","eligibility_conditions":"","regional_differences":"","important_exceptions":"","tax_year":"2026","sources":[{"title":"Rwanda - Individual - Other taxes","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/rwanda/individual/other-taxes","publisher":"PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"},{"title":"Rwanda - Corporate - Other taxes","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/rwanda/corporate/other-taxes","publisher":"PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"},{"title":"Rwanda - Individual - Taxes on personal income","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/rwanda/individual/taxes-on-personal-income","publisher":"PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"}],"verified_on":"2026-10-15","confidence":"low","verification":"partially_verified","open_questions":["Whether the listed-securities exemption covers foreign stock exchanges.","Whether gains on non-commercial (residential) property of individuals are taxed.","Treatment of foreign real estate gains."],"headline_rate":0.3,"rates":{"listed_securities_domestic":0.0,"listed_securities_foreign":0.1,"private_business_sale":0.1,"real_estate_local":0.3,"real_estate_foreign":null},"rate_basis":"Domestic listed: exempt (capital market transactions). Foreign listed: 10% assumed (worldwide basis; the listed exemption is read as the Rwandan capital market). Private business: 10%. Local real estate: 30% (commercial property; residential gains may be untaxed). Foreign real estate: null.","professional_trader":"Trading would be business income at up to 30%.","holding_period_rules":"","foreign_assets":"Worldwide taxation with credit for foreign tax up to the Rwandan tax."},"dividends":{"status":"researched","basis":"law_in_force","summary":"Dividends from Rwandan companies bear a 15% WHT that is the final tax; dividends on securities listed on the capital market paid to Rwandan or EAC residents bear 5%. Residents are taxed on worldwide income; foreign dividends are scored at the 30% top PIT rate with credit for foreign tax up to the Rwandan tax.","exemptions_thresholds":"","eligibility_conditions":"","regional_differences":"","important_exceptions":"","tax_year":"2026","sources":[{"title":"Rwanda - Individual - Income determination","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/rwanda/individual/income-determination","publisher":"PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"},{"title":"Rwanda - Corporate - Income determination","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/rwanda/corporate/income-determination","publisher":"PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"},{"title":"Rwanda - Corporate - Withholding taxes","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/rwanda/corporate/withholding-taxes","publisher":"PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"},{"title":"Rwanda - Individual - Taxes on personal inc